CHAPTER.VERS:
Is it a time for you

          {+}
         yourselves to dwell in your

          {+}
         ceiled houses, while this house lies waste?

Now therefore this is what Yahweh of Hosts says: Consider your

          {+}
         ways.

You

          {+}
         have sown much, and bring in little; you

          {+}
         eat, but you

          {+}
         don't have enough; you

          {+}
         drink, but you

          {+}
         are not filled with drink; you

          {+}
         clothe yourselves, but there is none warm; and he who earns wages, earns wages [to put it] into a bag with holes.

Thus says Yahweh of hosts: Consider your

          {+}
         ways.

You

          {+}
         looked for much, and, look, it came to little; and when you

          {+}
         brought it home, I blew on it. Why? says Yahweh of hosts. Because of my house that lies waste, while you

          {+}
         run every man to his own house.

Therefore above you

          {+}
         the heavens withhold the dew, and the earth withholds its fruit.

Then Haggai, Yahweh's messenger, spoke Yahweh's message to the people, saying, I am with you

          {+}
        , says Yahweh.
